So I eat this fortune cokie, and for the FIRST TIME I get a message that
is NOT:

1) A blindfold can be very useful if you're telepathic
    or:
2) A crystal plate mail will not rust

(BTW, O Great Dev Team, can you PLEASE randomize the fortune cookie
messages a BIT more?  I'm REEEEALY sick of reading those two.  There are
what, hundreds?  Jeez.)

Anyhow, the point is the message had something to do with Nazguls and a
Ring.  My question:  is there a possibility that my character will turn
into a Nazgul if I wear any ol' Ring O' Invisibility long enough, or was
this just to tell me 'Yes, Mike, there *is* a ring of invisibility.'  I
hope not.  That would *really* cap off how useless I feel the fortune
messages are.  Time was, one could get all kinds of cute -- and even,
occasionally, helpful -- messages (many written by Mr. Hairston! 
Thanks, Dave!) rather than these two annoying scraps o' paper I find
now.  It's to where I don't even bother with cookies anymore ('cept for
my compulsive nature which says, 'pick up everything in sight.  You may
need it later').

  Ah well.

